    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Jose Caballero** (80.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (78.36) leading the charge as our clear-cut priority starts. **Jose Caballero** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Corbin, with the dynamic platoon advantage providing a massive +13% boost to his efficiency score. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite facing the left-handed Abbott; his ability to impact the scarcest category (SB) while batting second ensures he remains near the top of our lineup output. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) and **Josh Naylor** (72.21) follow closely, both capitalizing on favorable matchups against Sugano and Poulin respectively. The high SP_xERA for these opposing arms creates a perfect environment for our core to produce across the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Kyle Karros**, whose 54.01 score fell just short of a recommended start despite his strong platoon edge. He was ultimately sidelined to prioritize the higher ceiling of **Max Muncy** (59.60), who maintains a superior base projection. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Dalton Rushing** (47.12) and **Alex Freeland** (49.51); while the wind blowing out provides a slight bump, both are flirting with our sub-50 marginal threshold. We are also closely monitoring the lineup security for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young**, as their scoring potential is heavily leveraged on their high spots in the batting order. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki** all unavailable, our depth is thin today, making it imperative that our remaining starters avoid late-inning defensive substitutions that could cap our volume.",
